.tile(data-name='Specification Editor' data-id='editor')
    .tile-image(style="background: url('images/app-editor.png') no-repeat;background-size:contain;")
    .tile-details
        .tile-title Specification Editor
        .tile-subtitle Define a product specification based on structured requirements with ease, enabling precise goals definition for your product development teams 
        .tile-access 
            .tile-endpoint /editor
            .tile-button.button.default(href="editor?wsid=143&dmsid=14435&working=true" target="_blank") Open
            .tile-button.button.icon.icon-start.default(href="https://youtu.be/tM8why6ybAU" target="_blank")
    .instructions
        h1 Features
        p Managing requirement structures in PLM can be a complex activity requiring many tabs and clicks. With this editor, creation of new requirements, edition of existing requirements and structural changes are by far easier to accomplish. Requirements will be defined in a familar experience, similar to management of Word Documents.
        ul
            li Use templates when creating new specifications
            li Paste Word contents to derive a requirement specification from a Word document
            li Edit requireents with rich text editing functionality
            li Change the structure easily (drag &amp; drop, indent button, outdent button)
            li Manage additional requirement details when needed
            li Side panel provides comprehensive information per requirement 
            li Maximize display of a single requirement to focus on proper requirement definition
            li Pinning capability makes navigation in structure easy
            li Reuse existing requirements from library
            li Launch the editor for a requirement or context object (ie. Product)
        p While this solution is focusing on management of requirements, its configuration settings enable reuse of the editor for other workspaces / use cases as well. Please review section 
            strong Configuration Settings 
            |for details.
        h1 Setup Instructions
        p This editor makes use of the standard 
            strong Requirements Management 
            |solution provided by all standard tenants and the Template Library. 
            br
            |However, multiple changes must be performed to workspace 
            strong Requirements 
            |to make this editor work properly.
        h2 Disable Requirements Specifications dependency for Requirements
        p As the editor does not use the 
            strong Requirements Specifications 
            |workspace for better usability, the dependency of requirements on this workspace must be removed per the steps described below.
        ol 
            li Edit script 
                strong Requirements onCreate
                |as shown below: Function setNumber must be changed to use a sequencer without reference to the specification. 
                img.border(src='images/apps/editor-5.png' style='max-width:580px;')
                p Copy / paste the following code:
                p.code 
                    span.indent-1 if(specID === null) {
                    span.indent-2 var seq = new Sequencer("Requirements");
                    span.indent-2 item.ID = "REQ-" + ('0000' + seq.nextValue().toString()).slice(-4);
                    span.indent-2 return;
                    span.indent-1 }        
            li In the 
                strong Requirements Item Details 
                | remove the 
                strong Selection Required 
                |validation of field 
                strong Related Specification 
                |by clicking the red X icon
                img.border(src='images/apps/editor-4.png' style='max-width:580px;')
        h2 Add Type Template 
        p To enable recognition of templates, the option 
            span.code Template 
            |must be added to picklist 
            strong Requirement Types
            |:
            img.border(src='images/apps/editor-6.png' style='max-width:580px;')
        p As the selected type drives the computed field Icon, add a new entry in the 
            strong Computed Field Formula 
            |of field 
            strong Icon 
            |as shown below. Note that the integer value matching the new entry Temmplate may be different from 67 in your environment.
            img.border(src='images/apps/editor-7.png' style='max-width:580px;')
        h2 Create new Item Details fields for Requirements
        p The editor can automatically lock library requirements to prevent accidential modifications. It can also flag requirements that are reused across multiple structures. However, both features require two additional fields that must be added to your 
            strong Requirements 
            |workspace. Add the two fields 
            strong Library Requirement 
            |and 
            strong Reused 
            |as shown in the screenshots below. Of course, you can also change the 
            strong Field names 
            |and even the 
            strong Field IDs 
            |by changing the application's Configuration Settings.
        table 
            tr 
                td 
                    img.border(src='images/apps/editor-1.png' style='max-width:580px;')
                td 
                    img.border(src='images/apps/editor-2.png' style='max-width:580px;')
        p You can add these fields to any section of your 
            strong Requirements 
            |workspace, for example to section
            strong Details
            |.
            img.border(src='images/apps/editor-3.png' style='max-width:320px;')
        h2 Create new BOM View for Requirements
        p The editor requires a new BOM view to retrieve all required information in a single request. Per standard configuration, this is accomplished by adding the new view 
            strong Editor 
            |for workspace 
            strong Requirements
            |. Of course, the BOM view to be used can be changed as described in the Cofiguration Settings chapter. 
        p Create this new BOM view and add the required columns (sequence of columns does not matter). Per standard configuration, the colums listed below are required. Once you change this application's Configuration Settings, this list might be different. In general, any field referenced in 
            span.code editor.requirements.wsMain 
            |should be added to this view.
        table.row-hovering 
            tr 
                th Field 
                th ID
                th Source 
                th Remark
            tr 
                td Descriptor
                td DESCRIPTOR
                td System Fields
                td Required
            tr 
                td Title
                td TITLE
                td Item Details [Basic] 
                td Required
            tr 
                td Description
                td DESCRIPTION
                td Item Details [Basic] 
                td Required
            tr 
                td Material Cost
                td MATERIAL_COST
                td Item Details [Cost &amp; Effort]
                td Optional (used by Advanced fields toggle)
            tr 
                td Tooling Cost
                td TOOLING_COST
                td Item Details [Cost &amp; Effort]
                td Optional (used by Advanced fields toggle)
            tr 
                td Effort [days]
                td EFFORT
                td Item Details [Cost &amp; Effort]
                td Optional (used by Advanced fields toggle)
            tr 
                td Test Procedure
                td TEST_PROCEDURE
                td Item Details [Validation]
                td Optional (used by Advanced fields toggle)
            tr 
                td Expected Result
                td EXPECTED_RESULT
                td Item Details [Validation]
                td Optional (used by Advanced fields toggle)
            tr 
                td Success Criteria
                td EXPECTED_RESULT
                td Item Details [Validation]
                td Optional (used by Advanced fields toggle)
            tr 
