        h2 Install Chrome Extension
        p The editor is launched by a new button being added to the header of requirements and workspace. This is accomplished by installing this UX package's Chrome Extensions, which must be installed on all clients that should use this new editor. Please click the button 
            strong Download the Chrome Extension 
            |on the left to download the required installer.
        a(href='/chrome' target='_blank') Learn more about the Chrome Extension
        h2 
        h1 Application Configuration Settings
        p The following application specific settings can be adjusted in your custom settings file in 
            span.code exports.applications.editor.requirements 
            br
            |In order to change any of these settings, copy the standard value from settings.js to your custom settings file in folder settings.
        table.row-hovering 
            tr 
                th Setting 
                th Default Value
                th Description 
            tr 
                td labels.appTitle
                td 'Requirements Editor'
                td The application title shown in the main toolbar
            tr 
                td labels.newTitle
                td 'New Requirements Structure Creation'
                td Title of the startup screen being displayed if there is no main item for the context object yet (ie if you launch the editor from a Product which does not have a Requirement linked yet)
            tr 
                td labels.addExisting
                td 'Add From Library'
                td Label of toggle and panel for addition of existing library requirements
            tr 
                td wsMain.workspaceId
                td null
                td Workspace ID of main workspace, the one used to build the structure. Provide the ID of your requirements workspace or set to null to automatically reuse the ID defined in exports.common.workspaceIds.requirements
            tr 
                td wsMain.workspaceName
                td 'Requirements'
                td Name to use for this main workspace
            tr 
                td wsMain.bomViewName
                td 'Editor'
                td BOM view of the main workspace to use for the structure expansion. This view must contain all required fields.
            tr 
                td wsMain.copyFromTemplate
                td [ 'TITLE', 'DESCRIPTION' ]
                td Array of fieldIds defining the fields to be copied from the requirement templates to their derived requirements
            tr 
                td wsMain.advancedFieldIds
                td [ .. ]
                td Array of fieldIds being accessible in 
                    strong Advanced Mode
                    |. These fields are hidden per default, but can be displayed when using the given toggle.
            tr 
                td wsMain.itemsLocked
                td { fieldId : .. , value : .. , title : .. }
                td Defines field and matching value for recognition of library requirements which will then be locked. Property title can be used to define the tooltip of the given icon being displayed in the editor for locked requirements.
            tr 
                td wsMain.itemsReused
                td { fieldId : .. , value : .. , title : .. }
                td Defines field and matching value for recognition and flagging of reused requirement. Property title can be used to define the tooltip of the given icon being displayed in the editor for reused requirements.
            tr 
                td wsMain.newDefaultValues
                td []
                td Array defining standard field values to be set for new requirements being created by the editor
            tr 
                td wsContexts
                td []
                td This array defines multiple context workspaces which can link to matching requirements and from which the editor should be accessible. 
            tr 
                td wsContexts[i].workspace
                td 'products'
                td Defines the context workspace ID by providing the matching name of the entry in 
                    span.code exports.common.workspaceIds 
            tr
                td wsContexts[i].fieldIds.link
                td 'REQUIREMENTS'
                td (Linking picklist) Field ID of context workspace refering to the related Requirements structure
            tr 
                td wsContexts[i].fieldIds.title
                td 'REQUIREMENTS'
                td Field ID of context workspace that will be used to derive the name of new structures being created
        p The standard configuration support the requirements editing use case only. However, you can also create further profiles and use the same editor also for BOM changes for example. To achieve this, copy the 
            span.code requirements 
            |property in 
            span.code exports.applications.editor 
            |and rename it to 
            span.code bom 
            |for example. Once the property 
            span.code exports.applications.editor 
            |has more than one configuration profile, you will then have to append a URL parameter to select the configuration profile to use. To launch the editor with your new profile 
            span.code bom
            |, you must append the following suffix to the URL of the editor: 
            span.code &amp;config=bom
            |. If the config URL parameter is not provided, the editor will use the first configuration profile found in 
            span.code exports.applications.editor
            |.
        h1 Panel Configuration Settings
        p This application uses multiple configurable panels which you can adjust to better meet your needs and tenant configuration.
            br  
            |You can use the 
            strong Panel Configuration Studio 
            |to explore these panels' features and derive the matching configuration settings.
            br
            a(href='studio?panel=insertSearch' target='_blank' style='margin:18px 0px;') Open Panel Configuration Studio
        p The application uses the panels listed below, which are all configured in property 
            span.code exports.applications.editor.requirements.panels
        table.row-hovering
            tr
                th Property 
                th Descripton
                th Panel Type
            tr 
                td ..panels.insertTemplates
                td Drives the list of available templates in startup screen when creating a new structure
                td insertResults
            tr 
                td ..panels.insertBOM
                td Drives the navigation tree on the left
                td insertBOM            
            tr 
                td ..panels.insertDetails
                td Configures the Details display in side panel 
                td insertDetails          
            tr 
                td ..panels.insertAttachments
                td Configures the Files display in side panel 
                td insertAttachments        
            tr 
                td ..panels.insertRelationships
                td Configures the Implemented By display in side panel 
                td insertRelationships         
            tr 
                td ..panels.insertChangeLog
                td Configures the Change Log display in side panel 
                td insertChangeLog            
            tr 
                td ..panels.insertWorkspaceSearch
                td Drives the Search panel in
                    strong Add From Library
                td insertWorkspaceSearch            
            tr 
                td ..panels.insertWorkspaceViews
                td Drives the Workspace Views panel in
                    strong Add From Library
                td insertWorkspaceViews            
            tr 
                td ..panels.insertBookmarks
                td Drives the Bookmarks panel in
                    strong Add From Library
                td insertBookmarks            
            tr 
                td ..panels.insertRecentItems
                td Drives the Recently Viewed panel in
                    strong Add From Library
                td insertRecentItems           
